  "_id": "index-burn",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "people of Lehi1 offer burnt offerings according to law of Moses, 1 Ne. 5:9 (7:22; Mosiah 2:3). many cities are burned with fire, 1 Ne. 12:4 (3 Ne. 8:14; 9:3, 9–10). day comes that wicked must be burned, 1 Ne. 22:15 (2 Ne. 26:4; 3 Ne. 25:1). the Lord purges by spirit of burning, 2 Ne. 14:4. wickedness burns as fire, 2 Ne. 19:18. main branches of olive tree cast into fire and burned, Jacob 5:7, 9. the Lord grieved that trees should be cut down and burned, Jacob 5:47. the Lord will cause vineyard to be burned, Jacob 5:77. world shall be burned with fire, Jacob 6:3. the Lord has seen fit to snatch Alma2 out of everlasting burning, Mosiah 27:28. Alma2 and Amulek not to be burned because work not finished, Alma 14:12–13. Nephi2 and Lehi4 are encircled by fire, but not burned, Hel. 5:23–24. the Lord will no longer accept burnt offerings, 3 Ne. 9:19. more righteous part of people are not burned, 3 Ne. 10:13. voice from heaven causes hearts to burn, 3 Ne. 11:3. day cometh that shall burn as oven, 3 Ne. 25:1 (Mal. 4:1). Nephites build cities where cities had been burned, 4 Ne. 1:7. Nephite cities burned by Lamanites, Morm. 5:5. Shiz burned cities, Ether 14:17.",
